id: torch
name: Torch
kind: gear
craftDC: Novice
# "You can spend 1 Action to turn on a Torch."
placeCost: 1
# "While you are holding a Torch, you are a Light Source. Increase the Light Level of all
# Squares within a Sphere AoE (centered on you) by 1 Level." The Torchlit mark on whoever
# holds it lit, which says which way and how far in its file.
lightMark: torchlit
source: Core Rule
description: >
  An Action to light it. Lit and in hand, it raises the Light Level around you by a Level.
text: >
  Torch: A handheld light source you can carry with you.
  –Craft DC: Novice
  –Effects: You can spend 1 Action to turn on a Torch. While you are holding a Torch, you are
  a Light Source. Increase the Light Level of all Squares within a Sphere AoE (centered on
  you) by 1 Level.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Light: 1 Action, and the holder is Torchlit for as long as it burns - their own Light Level a
# Level higher, read the way Brightened's is. Put out is free; the entry prices lighting it and
# nothing else. Put in a Capsule, or taken off the character, it goes out: "while you are
# holding a Torch".
#
# Two lit Torches are two Light Sources, and each raises the Level: "it increases the Light
# Level of an area by a certain value", with nothing said about more than one.
#
# --- What the table keeps ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The rest of the Sphere. It is centred on the holder and moves with them, over Squares this
# system does not have - so everyone else in it raises their own Light Level on the
# Battlefields tab, the way every other Light Level here is set.
